Z||000000||Gokart||07-10-2000||06:53 AM|||| <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=378642923&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=378642923&r=0&t=0</A>  I don't remember seeing this on my GT the few hundred times I've been under my car over the last year! I wonder if it helps keep water from coming down on the manifold as well as a heat sheild? I'll be getting my ported/welded set soon from Tom and was wondering if I should seek out one of these before I do the swap?<P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||sdm1964||07-10-2000||06:59 AM||||I beleive that he is talking about the long heatshield. It usually has burns to it and is removed. good deal for 5 bucks||||reg||5
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||07-10-2000||01:43 PM||||It is OEM but it is true that not all V6s have it. It seems to be an overkill from GM to protect the manifolf from any oil that would leak from the valve covers. Of the cars that we have seen without this shield, we have seen no problems. <P>Bottom line: It came from the factory. You can have it but you don't need it||||reg||1
